WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.639
A quick phone call to a colleague nearby.

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:07.590
Everyone in the neighborhood is waiting for
an electricity worker to arrive.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:12.339
With the flick of a switch, they turn off
electricity in one neighborhood, and power

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:13.889
up somewhere else.

00:00:13.889 --> 00:00:17.750
Gaza is getting very little electricity from
the Israeli grid.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:22.230
"My colleague here was waiting for a call
from someone at the Eastern line to switch

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.550
on the electricity.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:28.080
What happened is he just shut off the connection
from the Western side because this neighborhood's

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.840
turn is over."

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.210
Just a few streets away, Maisa Sultan is hurrying
to fill the washing machine.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:40.539
Her neighborhood has electricity again – but
only for a precious three hours a day.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.620
All of that in the middle of the summer.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:48.420
“When the electricity comes on, I start
washing my laundry, and do anything else I

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.920
need energy for.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:56.179
I have to do this all very quickly.“
Even the makeshift battery system, which supplies

00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:59.300
a little light during a blackout, needs to
be charged.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.159
Nothing works - refrigerators, water pumps,
elevators.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:11.189
Last week, the two million inhabitants of
Gaza had to make do with as little as two

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:12.719
hours of power every day.

00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:17.150
“The situation is going from bad to worse.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:23.370
But if our self-proclaimed leaders in Gaza
and the West Bank would not just consider

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:28.649
their own interests, but finally take the
wishes of the people into account, then something

00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:37.659
might change.“
Gaza has been blockaded by Israel and Egypt

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:39.490
for more than a decade.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:44.540
In April, Gaza's only power plant had to be
shut down because of a lack of fuel.

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.390
Since then, Gaza has depended on energy from
Egypt and Israel.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:54.479
But last week, Israel reduced its electricity
supply at the request of Palestinian president

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:55.479
Mahmoud Abbas.

00:01:55.479 --> 00:01:59.829
He's no longer wants to pay the power bill
for the Gaza Strip, which is controlled by

00:01:59.829 --> 00:02:01.509
his rival Hamas.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:07.109
„The sole alternative is for Hamas to respond
to the initiative of the President by handing

00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:11.709
over the border crossings, reverting from
its coup and by handing over all government

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:14.870
institutions to the government of national
consensus.”

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:20.430
Hamas is under further pressure, because Qatar,
one of its main sponsors, is having problems

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.630
of its own.

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:28.019
Since 2014, the gulf state had been funding
streets, hospitals and even fuel.

00:02:28.019 --> 00:02:33.890
“It is clear that the main cause of this
impasse is the Israeli occupation, in cooperation

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.620
with President Abbas.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:37.950
People should protest against those behind
the blockade.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:42.450
We are telling our people that they have to
tolerate more of this reality.”

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:49.361
On Gaza’s coastline, one can smell the fallout
of the crisis long before one sees it: This

00:02:49.361 --> 00:02:54.319
is where the sewage from millions of Gazans
is flushed into the Mediterranean Sea.

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:58.379
The dirty water then flows north, towards
Israel.

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:04.690
“We're talking about 100,000 cubic meters
of sewage water, that reaches the beach.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:09.879
It's either only partially purified or not
at all.”

00:03:09.879 --> 00:03:15.040
And while Egypt recently delivered a small
amount of fuel to the Gaza Strip, that shipment

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.650
was just a drop in the bucket in an ever-worsening
crisis.

